    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Well, one thing that I think is a dynamic, especially coming out of these off-year elections, so I think people are overreying it a bit. You know, is this fear on the part of the DC consultant class and a lot of donors that, you know, Republican, their allegiance to the pro life cause is something that is proving to be a significant detriment. Now, I know that that's something that, you know, is I mean, something that they've tried to peel away in a lot of different ways over the last couple of decades. Obviously, you're someone who's become prominent for standing on this issue. What do you say to your colleagues who basically say, can't we just tamper things down. Can't we just avoid talking about this? We'd rather talk about, you know, popular things like cutting Medicare for people or something like that. You know, pick your poison. What's your response to the folks who basically just say, you know, you're highlighting an issue we don't want to talk about?",
